/* book exam traps: Adsorption is not absorption: the solute stays on the pore walls of the solid; in absorption it dissolves into the whole liquid. | Using V = 100 with mg/L gives 4000 mg instead of 4.0 mg. Convert mL to L. | q is mass of solute per mass of dry adsorbent, not a concentration in the liquid. | Physical adsorption falls as temperature rises because it is exothermic; that is the basis of regeneration by heating. | A zeolite does not split O2 from N2 by sieving size: both enter, and N2 is held more strongly. The carbon molecular sieve is the one that separates by rate. */
